hadiths[63]{hadithnumber,text}:
"697","Chapter 71: The book of marriage. 729 - Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from 'Umarah ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from 'Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: O company of youths, whoever of you is able to marry, let him marry, for it lowers the gaze and guards chastity; and whoever is not able, fasting is upon him, for it is a restraint for him."
"698","730 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us. And Abu Ja'far al-Mukharrami Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibacy."
"699","731 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: 'Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Ibn al-Musayyib narrated to him, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who informed him, he said: 'Uthman ibn Maz'un wanted to live celibate, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade him. Sa'd said: Had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted that to him, we would have castrated ourselves."
"700","732 - 'Ali ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Bakr ibn 'Abdillah al-Muzani, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I proposed to a woman, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Did you look at her? He said: I said: No. He said: Then look at her, for it is more likely to bring affection between you."
"701","733 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah proposed to a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go and look at her, for it is more lasting for what is between you."
"702","734 - 'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, Ibn 'Uyaynah said. And Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and 'Ali said: He raises it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: Do not practice najsh, and let no resident sell for a Bedouin, and let no man sell over the sale of his brother, and let no man propose over the proposal of his brother, and let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister. 'Ali added: So as to overturn what is in her vessel."
"703","735 - Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not fitting for a woman to stipulate the divorce of her sister so as to overturn her vessel."
"704","736 - Abu Zur'ah al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: 'Abthar informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the tashahhud in prayer, and the tashahhud in need; then he mentioned the tashahhud in prayer and the tashahhud in need, and said: And the tashahhud in need is that one says: Indeed all praise belongs to Allah; we praise Him, seek His help, and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls; whomever Allah guides, none can misguide, and whomever He misguides, none can guide; and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he recites three verses of the Qur'an: {Fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims}. {And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs; indeed Allah is ever watchful over you}. {O you who believe, fear Allah and speak a right word}."
"705","737 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Nufayli narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from 'Urwah, from Zaynab bint Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, that Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of Allah, do you desire my sister? He said: What would I do? She said: You marry her. He said: Your sister? She said: Yes. He said: And do you love that? She said: I am not alone, and the one I most love to share good with me is my sister! He said: Then she is not lawful to me. She said: By Allah, I have been told that you are proposing to Durrah - or Dharrah, the doubt is from Zuhayr. He said: The daughter of Umm Salamah? She said: Yes. He said: By Allah, had she not been my stepdaughter under my care, she would not have been lawful to me; she is the daughter of my foster-brother; Thuwaybah nursed me and her father, so do not present your daughters or your sisters to me."
"706","738 - Rawh ibn al-Faraj, the freedman of Muhammad ibn Sabiq, narrated to us, he said: 'Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara', from his father, he said: I met my uncle with a banner fastened, so I said: Where are you heading? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married his father's wife, to strike his neck and take his wealth."
"707","739 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Rifa'ah al-Qurazi, from al-Zubayr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, that Rifa'ah ibn Samaw'al divorced his wife Tumaymah bint Wahb in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr married her, but was unable to consummate with her, so he divorced her without touching her; then Rifa'ah wanted to marry her - and he was her husband who had divorced her before 'Abd al-Rahman - so that was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade him to marry her, saying: She is not lawful to you until she tastes the sweetness."
"708","740 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the wife of Rifa'ah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Rifa'ah divorced me with a divorce by which I became irrevocable from him, and I married 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr, and he is with him like the fringe of a garment. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and said: Do you want to return to Rifa'ah? No, until he tastes your sweetness and you taste his sweetness."
"709","741 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us. And Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla informed us, from 'Abdillah ibn Ja'far - that is al-Mukharrimi - from 'Uthman ibn Muhammad, from al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has cursed the muhallil and the one for whom it is done."
"710","742 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Dawud - meaning Ibn Abi Hind - informed us, he said: 'Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt, and the paternal aunt over her brother's daughter, or a woman over her maternal aunt, or the maternal aunt over her sister's daughter; the younger is not married over the elder, nor the elder over the younger."
"711","743 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Jabir ibn 'Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave who marries without the permission of his master and his family is a fornicator."
"712","744 - Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fosterage makes unlawful what birth makes unlawful."
"713","745 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya informed us that 'Amrah, the daughter of 'Abd al-Rahman, informed him that she heard 'A'ishah saying: There was revealed in the Qur'an ten known sucklings, meaning what makes unlawful from fosterage. 'Amrah said: Then 'A'ishah mentioned and said: Afterwards five were revealed."
"714","746 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Wuhayb, from Ayyub, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from 'Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One or two sucks do not make unlawful."
"715","747 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: The nephew of Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from his uncle, he said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Sahlah bint Suhayl ibn 'Amr came - and she was under Abu Hudhayfah ibn 'Utbah - and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon us while I am in light dress, and we used to consider him a son; and Abu Hudhayfah had adopted him just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) adopted Zayd, then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: {Call them by their fathers; that is more just with Allah}. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then ordered her to nurse Salim, so she nursed him five sucklings, and he became like her son by fosterage. For that reason 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to order her brothers and the daughters of her brothers to nurse whomsoever 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, loved to see her and enter upon her, even if grown, five sucklings, then he would enter upon her; while Umm Salamah and the rest of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused that anyone enter upon them by that nursing, until he is nursed in the cradle, and they said to 'A'ishah: By Allah, we do not know; perhaps it was a concession from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for Salim apart from people."
"716","748 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from al-Ash'ath, from his father, from Masruq, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while a man was with her, and said: Who is this? She said: My brother by fosterage. He said: Look to who your brothers are, for fosterage is only from hunger."
"717","749 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah. 750 - And Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her - one of them adding to the other - she said: My uncle came after the veil was imposed, asking permission to enter upon me, but I did not permit him; then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, so I asked him, and he said: Permit him, for he is your uncle. I said: Only the woman nursed me, and the man did not nurse me? He said: May your right hand be dusted, permit him, for he is your uncle."
"718","751 - 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both. And 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: Qatadah narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The daughter of Hamzah, may Allah be pleased with him, was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: She is the daughter of my brother by fosterage."
"719","752 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Nubayh ibn Wahb, the brother of Banu 'Abd al-Dar, that 'Umar ibn 'Abdillah wanted to marry Talhah ibn 'Umar to the daughter of Shaybah ibn Jubayr while both were in ihram, so he sent to Aban ibn 'Uthman ibn 'Affan to attend that. He said: So Aban disapproved of that to him, while he was the leader of the pilgrimage, and Aban said: I heard 'Uthman ibn 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one in ihram does not marry, nor give in marriage, nor propose."
"720","753 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, the nephew of Maymunah, from Maymunah bint al-Harith, that she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me at Sarif while we were both lawful."
"721","754 - Ibn al-Muqri and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Amr, from Abu al-Sha'tha', that Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while he was in ihram."
"722","754/2 - So I informed al-Zuhri of it, and he said: Yazid ibn al-Asamm informed me - and she is his maternal aunt - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while he was lawful, and she was lawful."
"723","755 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan and 'Abdillah, the two sons of Muhammad - he said: And al-Hasan was the more reliable of them - from their father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage, and the meat of domestic donkeys at the time of Khaybar. And Sufyan used to say: al-Hasan was the better of them."
"724","756 - Ibn al-Muqri said: And Sufyan narrated it to us with it another time and mentioned it, and said: From their father, he heard 'Ali saying to Ibn 'Abbas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage, and the meat of domestic donkeys."
"725","757 - Ibn al-Muqri and Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah al-Juhani, from his father: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage."
"726","758 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, he said: al-Rabi' ibn Sabrah al-Juhani narrated to us, from his father, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when we completed our 'umrah, he said to us: Enjoy yourselves with these women - and enjoyment with us that day was marriage. He said: So we presented that to the women, but they refused unless we fixed a term between us and them. He said: So we mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do so. He said: So I and a cousin of mine went out, with me a cloak and with him a cloak, and his cloak was better than mine, and I was younger than him. He said: So we came to a woman and presented that to her, and my youth pleased her, while my cousin's cloak pleased her, so she said: A cloak like a cloak. So I married her, and the term between me and her was ten days. He said: So I spent that night with her, then I went in the morning to the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) standing, delivering a sermon between the Hijr and the Door, saying: O people, I had permitted you enjoyment with these women; but Allah has forbidden that until the Day of Resurrection, so whoever has any of them with him, let him release her, and do not take anything of what you gave them."
"727","759 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa informed me that Ibn Shihab informed him that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him that 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is void; if he enters with her, she has the dowry for what he made lawful of her private part; and if they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian."
"728","760 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: Qabisah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"729","761 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"730","762 - Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn 'Askar narrated to us, he said: 'Amr ibn 'Uthman al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"731","763 - Abu Bakr Hamdan ibn Muhammad ibn Raja' ibn al-Sindi and Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Jawhari narrated to us, they said: Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. 764 - And Sharik also joined it and attributed it."
"732","765 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ishaq said, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Zubayr narrated it to me, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq, Juwayriyah bint al-Harith fell in the share of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, or a cousin of his. He said: So she contracted kitabah for herself, and she was a sweet, charming woman; hardly anyone saw her without being captivated by her. So she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help for her kitabah. She said: By Allah, it was only that I saw her at the door of the chamber and disliked her, and I knew he would see in her what I saw. So she said: O Messenger of Allah, I am Juwayriyah the daughter of al-Harith ibn Abi Dirar, the chief of his people, and there has befallen me of the affair what is not hidden from you, so I fell in the share of Thabit, or a cousin of his, and I contracted kitabah for myself, so I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his help for my kitabah. He said: Do you have something better than that? She said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I pay your kitabah and marry you? She said: Yes. He said: I have done so. And the news went out among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, so the people said: The in-laws of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so they released what was in their hands of the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq. His marrying her freed one hundred households of Banu al-Mustaliq; we know no woman who was a greater blessing upon her people than her."
"733","766 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Ibn Abi Salamah, he said: Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: I heard something from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which is more pleasing to me than such-and-such: No one is afflicted with a calamity, and he mentioned part of the hadith. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her and proposed to her, so she said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). In me are three traits which I fear for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a woman of intense jealousy, I am a woman none of my guardians is present to marry me, and I am a woman with children. So 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, heard of that and became angry for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more intensely than he became angry for himself when she said to him: O son of al-Khattab, in me is such-and-such. So what she said reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he came to her and said: As for what you mentioned of your jealousy, I shall supplicate Allah, exalted, to remove it from you; and as for what you mentioned of your children, Allah will suffice them; and as for what you mentioned that there is here none of your guardians to marry you, there is none of your guardians, present or absent, who dislikes me. So she said to her son: Marry the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he married her to him."
"734","767 - Abu Ja'far al-Darimi narrated to us and said: 'Abd al-Samad ibn 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, they said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously-married woman is not married until she is consulted, and a virgin is not married until she is asked permission. It was said: And what is her permission, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That she remains silent. The hadith is al-Darimi's."
"735","768 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Mukharrami and 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating, from Dhakwan Abu 'Amr, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet, he said: Seek permission. And al-Mukharrami said: Consult women regarding their private parts. It was said: But the virgin is shy and remains silent? He said: Then her silence is her permission. And al-Mukharrami said: She is shy. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then it is her permission."
"736","769 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from 'Abdillah ibn al-Fadl, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr ibn Mut'im, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A previously-married woman has more right over herself than her guardian, and a virgin is consulted regarding herself, and her silence is her consent."
"737","770 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And in what I read to Ibn Nafi', from Malik, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from 'Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi', the two sons of Yazid ibn Jariyah al-Ansari, from Khansa' bint Khidham al-Ansariyyah, may Allah be pleased with them both: That her father married her off while she was previously married, and she disliked that, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he annulled her marriage."
"738","771 - Harun ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: 'Abdah narrated to us, from Hisham, from his father, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six years old, and consummated with me when I was nine years old."
"739","772 - al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, from Sulayman - meaning Ibn Bilal - from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Habib, that he heard 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah saying: Yusuf ibn Mahak informed me that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three, their seriousness is seriousness and their jest is seriousness: marriage, divorce, and return."
"740","773 - Yahya ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Umm Habibah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while she was in the land of Abyssinia; al-Najashi married her to him and gave her a dowry of four thousand, and prepared her from his own, and sent her with Shurahbil ibn Hasanah; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not send anything to her. And the dowry of his wives was four hundred dirhams."
"741","774 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, with this chain, similar to it."
"742","775 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us that he heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, married a woman of the Ansar, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: How much did you give her as dowry? He said: A date-stone of gold. Ibn Abi Najih said: The nawah is five dirhams, the nashsh is twenty dirhams, and the uqiyyah is forty dirhams."
"743","776 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, he said: While we were among the people, a woman said: I have given myself to you, O Messenger of Allah! Give your opinion about me! So a man stood and said: Marry her to me! He said: Go and seek, even an iron ring. He said: So he went and did not bring anything, not even an iron ring. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have anything of the chapters of the Qur'an with you? He said: Yes. He said: So he married her to him for what he had of the chapters of the Qur'an."
"744","777 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Bishr - meaning Ibn al-Sari - narrated to us, from Dawud - meaning Ibn Qays - from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Our dowry when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us was ten uqiyyahs."
"745","778 - Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman - meaning Ibn Mahdi - informed us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdillah. And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us - and the hadith is his - he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from 'Alqamah, from 'Abdillah, regarding a man who married a woman and did not stipulate for her nor touch her until he died. He said: So he turned them away, then said: I say about it by my opinion; if it is correct, it is from Allah, and if it is wrong, it is from me: I see for her the dowry of a woman of her women, neither deficient nor excessive, and upon her is the waiting period, and for her is inheritance. He said: So Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: I bear witness that you have judged in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Barwa' bint Washiq - a woman of Banu Ruwas - and Banu Ruwas is a clan of Banu 'Amir ibn Sa'sa'ah."
"746","779 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"747","780 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: And in what I read to Ibn Nafi', from Malik ibn Anas, from Nafi', from 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar. And shighar is that a man marries a man his daughter on condition that the other marries him his daughter, with no dowry between them."
"748","781 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Hisham - meaning Ibn Hassan - he said: Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"749","782 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man has two wives and inclines to one of them, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides fallen."
"750","783 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, 'Alqamah ibn Waqqas al-Laythi, and 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Utbah ibn Mas'ud informed me of the hadith of 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet, said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to travel, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out with her."
"751","784 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Sunnah is that when one marries a virgin, he stays with her seven days, and when he marries a previously-married woman, he stays with her three days."
"752","785 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Yunus ibn Yazid informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to him that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to travel, he would cast lots among his wives; whichever one's lot came out, he would go out with her with him. And he used to allot to each of his women her day and her night, except that Sawdah bint Zam'ah gave her day and her night to 'A'ishah, seeking thereby the pleasure of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"753","786 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf married, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Hold a wedding feast, even with a sheep."
"754","787 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Hafsah, or one of his wives, and held a wedding feast for her of dates and sawiq."
"755","788 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Usamah ibn al-Hadi, from 'Umarah ibn Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah is not shy of the truth; do not come to women in their backs."
"756","789 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn 'Uthman, from Makhramah ibn Sulayman, from Kurayb, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not look at a man who comes to a man or a woman in the back passage."
"757","790 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: 'Abd ibn Zam'ah and Sa'd disputed about the son of the slave-woman of Zam'ah. Sa'd said: My brother advised me, when I come to Mecca, to take the son of the slave-woman of Zam'ah, for he is my son. So 'Abd ibn Zam'ah said: The son of my father's slave-woman, born on my father's bed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a clear resemblance to 'Utbah, and said: He is yours, O 'Abd ibn Zam'ah; and the child belongs to the bed; and veil yourself from him, O Sawdah."
"758","791 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abdillah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abu Marzuq al-Tujibi, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Ruwayfi' ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not lawful for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day - or whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not water his water the child of another."
"759","792 - Muhammad ibn 'Awf narrated to us, he said: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar the meat of donkeys, and every beast of prey with fangs, and that captive women be approached until they give birth."
